<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="esculetin biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260303222105">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-5349" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;b&gt;ARACYC&lt;/b&gt; The presence of this pathway in Arabidopsis has been inferred based on the observation of esculetin in Arabidopsis metabolite profiles (Sumner L, personal communication). &lt;b&gt;METACYC&lt;/b&gt; Esculetin is a common coumarin that may form nonenzymatically from caffeic acid|CITS: [13806518]|. Nevertheless, enzymatic catalysis has been observed with a phenolase from &lt;i&gt;Saxifraga stolonifera&lt;/i&gt;|CITS: [Sato67]|. Further involvement of enzymes beyond phenolase has not been determined. The isomerization reactions are likely spontaneous, while involvement of enzymes in hydroxylation and dehydroxylation reactions remains uncertain. As neither caffeate or esculetin have been reported from &lt;i&gt;S. stolonifera&lt;/i&gt;, this pathway is likely relevant only for other plant species.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE" />
    <Author name="walk" />
  </Authors>
